Which framework are you using? The pattern is similar across most: load the title synchronously (or via a tiny parallel request) and stream/suspend the rest.

For example, in **Remix/React Router**, put the title in `clientLoader` as returned (non-deferred) data and defer the heavy payload:

```ts
export async function clientLoader({ params }) {
  const title = await fetchProjectTitle(params.id)
  const rest = fetchProject(params.id) // not awaited
  return defer({ title, rest })
}
```

Render `title` immediately, wrap the heavy parts in `<Await resolve={rest}>` so they stream in without blocking navigation.

In **Next.js App Router**, scope the title into a `layout.tsx` (or use a parallel route / `loading.tsx`) so the route shell with the title streams first while dynamic segments fetch the rest.

What stack are you on? I can give the exact setup.
